{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said to Moses: Do not fear him.</b> Rashi explained that Moses was afraid lest the merit of Abraham stand for him — for if not, it is difficult: was Moses afraid of a scion of flesh and blood, when HaShem was with him? And there is a further difficulty: since it says ״כִּי בְיָדְךָ נָתַתִּי אוֹתוֹ וְאֶת עַמּוֹ״, if so, He should have said 'Do not fear him and his people'; rather, surely he was not afraid of his people, for HaShem was with him, but of him alone he was afraid, lest the merit of Abraham stand for him." "And as for what they press here — how could he have been afraid of this merit? On the contrary, at that time he was a sinner and a great rebel, for his intention was that Abraham be killed and he would take Sarah for himself, as Rashi explained there (Genesis 14:13). This is no difficulty, for Rashi explained it thus according to the truth: for at the end of the matter, it is heard in all things that this merit availed him nothing, and if so, his end proves that his intention was for evil and not for good. But Moses did not yet know the end of the matter, and he supposed that his intent was for his benefit, to save Lot; therefore he was afraid lest this merit stand for him. And the Holy One, blessed be He, answered him: ״אַל תִּירָא אוֹתוֹ כִּי בְיָדְךָ נָתַתִּי״ — and He should have said ״כִּי בְיָדְךָ אֶתֵּן״ in the future tense; although HaShem's giving is as though it were already given, nevertheless in a place where it can be explained according to its plain sense there is no need for this explanation. And the explanation of the matter is: from long ago I have already given him into your hand, for never did he have any merit, and in that deed he was pursued to his destruction, and his intention was for evil, and it was decreed upon him from of old that he would be given to you and delivered into your hand. And this is a precious interpretation."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:42:22.248526202Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}